# The locale tooling in EverythingLocales writes LF, but a fresh clone under
# core.autocrlf=true checks out CRLF, so regenerating a locale reported every line as
# changed and buried the real edit. Pinning authored Lua to LF ends that.
*.lua text eol=lf

# Vendored third-party code keeps whatever core.autocrlf gives it. Both attributes have to
# be unset - 'eol' on its own still forces conversion - and '!' unsets rather than '-',
# which would instead turn conversion off and rewrite these to LF.
Libs/** !text !eol
